Assumptions.Assumption:
**The mechanism facts (read 2026-09-17 at `b6d7aba`; expires).** `nextEventId`
(`src/grace-cursor.ts:3337`) is a read-then-return with no reservation;
`writeEventFile` (`:3282`) writes `<id>-<task>-<kind>.xml`;
`EVENT_FILENAME` (`src/artifact/run-membership.ts:48`) makes the filename id-plus-task-plus-kind,
so an exclusive create on the final name catches only the same-task class;
`validateEventsAgainstAllocations` (`src/grace-cursor.ts:2810`) checks membership, holes and
the closer but never duplicate ids, which is why `recover` prints `Fold: ok`. The projected
mechanism is the plan's to choose; these are the constraints it must satisfy, not a mandated
implementation.
